{"raw": {"https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4529532": {"title": "People and Payroll Specialist", "description": "People and Payroll Specialist. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description The People and Payroll Specialist administers the College's payroll accurately, timely, and confidentially, and provides operational support across the Office of People, Success & Opportunity. The position is a primary resource for faculty, staff, student employees, supervisors, administrators, and job candidates on payroll, employee records, onboarding, benefits, and employment processes. The role requires exceptional attention to detail, discretion with sensitive information, sound judgment, and the ability to manage recurring deadlines alongside competing priorities. Essential Job Responsibilities: Payroll processing. Prepares, inputs, transmits, and verifies biweekly payroll and manual checks for faculty, staff, and student employees. Reviews timekeeping, attendance, leave, overtime, stipends, supplemental pay, and deductions for accuracy. Ensures payroll is completed within established deadlines. Payroll review and reconciliation. Reviews payroll registers and related reports, reconciles payroll data, and researches and resolves discrepancies. Coordinates payroll reconciliation with the Business Office. Assists with year-end processes, including W-2 preparation, review, distribution, and reconciliation. Employee changes and deductions. Processes new hires, salary changes, promotions, transfers, leaves, terminations, and other status changes affecting pay. Administers and tracks garnishments, retirement and TIAA contributions, insurance and HSA deductions, accrued leave, and other payroll-related items, ensuring each is accurately reflected in employee records. Faculty and adjunct compensation. Tracks faculty work and allocates it to contract, adjunct, or other applicable compensation categories. Prepares adjunct payroll through a multi-tiered payment process, coordinates payment for independent study courses, and generates contracts for (WOL) undergraduate adjunct faculty following established census dates. Verifies assignments and compensation with academic departments and administrators. Onboarding and employment administration . Coordinates and completes onboarding for new faculty, staff, temporary, and student employees, including required forms, deadlines, and orientation to College policies and procedures. Verifies I-9 documentation and submits to E-Verify, reports new hires to the State of Indiana, and enters background check information in the designated system. Monitors outstanding requirements and follows up with employees, supervisors, and departments. Recruitment support. Posts College job openings through appropriate recruitment channels, routes application materials to hiring personnel, responds to candidate inquiries about the employment process, and maintains related documentation. Employee records and data management. Maintains confidential personnel files and employment records in accordance with College policy and applicable requirements. Supports data integrity across payroll, employee information, timekeeping, and benefits systems, reviewing for completeness and resolving discrepancies. Reporting. Prepares routine and specialized reports on employee data, payroll, compensation, benefits, and employment activity for the Office of People, Success & Opportunity and other departments as appropriate. Benefits administration support. Inputs, monitors, and tracks benefit elections and deductions; reconciles benefits statements and resolves discrepancies; processes benefit changes; assists with annual enrollment and related communications; answers routine benefit questions and refers complex questions to the appropriate provider or College resource. Supports tracking of applicable leave programs, including FMLA, and assists with Workers' Compensation claims. Employee service. Serves as a responsive resource for faculty, staff, student employees, and supervisors on payroll and employment processes. Explains pay statements, deductions, leave balances, timekeeping, benefits, deadlines, and the Employee Self-Service system clearly, and works with employees and supervisors to research and resolve issues. Maintains confidentiality in all interactions. Compliance and audit support. Maintains compliance with federal, state, and local payroll, tax, employment, and recordkeeping requirements. Gathers, organizes, and provides documentation for the annual audit, Workers' Compensation audits, Social Security reporting, and other internal and external reviews within established deadlines. Monitors regulatory changes and communicates relevant updates to the Office. Policy and performance process support . Provides administrative support for the performance review process, including tracking deadlines, distributing materials, and maintaining documentation. Assists with updates to the staff and faculty handbooks, compensation policies, forms, and employee resources, and supports related employee communications. Campus collaboration. Works with the Business Office, Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, supervisors, and department leaders to support the payroll and employment needs of all employee classifications. Develops working knowledge of the College's academic calendar, census dates, payroll schedules, and employee classifications. Supports projects and process improvements as assigned. Campus mail and package services. Processes incoming and outgoing campus mail and packages. Picks up mail and packages from the local post office and transports them to campus. Sorts and distributes incoming mail and packages to departments across campus, coordinating with campus offices on mail and package needs as they arise. Performs other duties as assigned Other Duties & Responsibilities: Work requires tact, discretion and confidentiality Able to handle multifunctional tasks Ability to meet deadlines Capable of working in a fast-paced environment Supervision: May supervise student workers Requirements Required Qualifications Associate degree in business, accounting, finance, office administration, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Three or more years of experience in payroll, accounting, employee administration, or a closely related field, including direct payroll processing responsibility. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel. Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Strong organizational, time-management, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment with sensitive employee, payroll, and personal information. Ability to work independently, prioritize competing responsibilities, and meet recurring deadlines. Ability to work effectively with individuals at all levels of the College and with a diverse population of employees and students. Ability to learn and navigate payroll, HRIS, timekeeping, and other College software systems. Valid driver's license and ability to travel locally for mail and package duties. Preferred Qualifications Payroll processing experience in higher education. Experience with faculty, adjunct, and student payroll. Experience coordinating onboarding, I-9 and E-Verify processes, and employment background checks. Experience with an HRIS, payroll, timekeeping, or employee information system. Experience with benefits administration and reconciliation. Experience supporting FMLA and Workers' Compensation processes. Experience with payroll reconciliation, reporting, and audit preparation. Knowledge of federal and Indiana payroll and tax requirements. Payroll or related professional certification (FPC, CPP, PHR, SHRM-CP, or similar). Working Conditions: Office environment"}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3982553": {"title": "Associate Director of Student Success", "description": "Associate Director of Student Success. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description Saint Mary-of-the-Woods College (SMWC), a Catholic liberal arts institution founded by the Sisters of Providence, seeks an energetic, student-centered Associate Director of Student Success to lead initiatives that promote student achievement, persistence, and belonging. The Associate Director will oversee the College\u2019s Summer Bridge Program and the 21st Century Scholars Program, ensuring that underrepresented, first-generation, and conditionally admitted students are supported through their transition to and success in college. Working under the direction of the Director of Student Services for Student Success, the Associate Director provides leadership in designing, implementing, and assessing academic support initiatives that align with institutional goals for retention, equity, and holistic student development. Program Leadership and coordination Plan, implement, and assess the Summer Bridge Program, focusing on academic readiness, college transition, and community building for incoming students. Serve as the campus lead for the 21st Century Scholars Program, ensuring compliance with state requirements and supporting student engagement, persistence, and completion. Collaborate with Academic Affairs, Student Life, and Admissions to identify and support students who may benefit from early or ongoing academic interventions. Develop and coordinate academic workshops, mentoring programs, and co-curricular initiatives that promote student success and belonging. Collect, track, and analyze data on program participation, retention, and outcomes; prepare reports and use data for continuous improvement. Student Success and Support Provide individualized academic coaching and success planning for students participating in the Summer Bridge or 21st Century Scholars programs. Serve as a resource for students navigating academic challenges, referring them to tutoring, counseling, advising, and other campus resources. Build strong relationships with students to foster engagement, confidence, and persistence. Collaborate with faculty and staff to create a supportive and inclusive learning environment. Assist the Director of the LRC in supervising student employees, peer mentors, and/or professional tutors connected to bridge or scholar programs. Develop program budgets and monitor expenditures in alignment with institutional and grant guidelines. Contribute to LRC assessment, reporting, and strategic planning efforts. Participate in campus committees and initiatives that advance academic support and student success Supervision: Student Assistants and Academic Peers Working Conditions: Normal office environment Some evening and weekend hours Same day business travel as needed Overnight business travel as needed Performing repetitive movements Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree - Master\u2019s degree Preferred Minimum of two years of experience in student success, academic support, or program coordination in a higher education setting. Demonstrated commitment to working with first-generation, underrepresented, and at-risk college students. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Experience with program assessment and data-informed decision making."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4510227": {"title": "Director of Financial Aid", "description": "Director of Financial Aid. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description The Director of Financial Aid is responsible for the management and administration of the student Financial Aid Office and its functions, including but not limited to accounting operations, budget preparation, preparation of Federal, state and district reports, maintenance of Federal fund budgetary controls and regulatory compliance, and the delivery of funds and services to students. The Director maintains compliance with all federal, state and local regulations governing student aid programs. Essential Job Responsibilities: Directs and coordinates the delivery of student financial aid and the maintenance of student financial aid records. Recommends, interprets, administers and updates financial aid policies ensuring compliance with pertinent federal, state and local laws and contractual regulations. Oversees the institutions Program Participation Agreement (PPA), including updates and recertifications, the SAIG mailbox, Scholartrack and prepares various surveys, waivers and grants. Ensures proper and compliant awarding and disbursement of federal, state and institutional student financial aid according to regulations. Works closely with the VP for Enrollment Management, the President and CFO regarding available funds from student financial aid sources. Ensures all federal/state and institutional processes are being performed efficiently, accurately and timely. Coordinates financial aid operations with other appropriate college offices, including Admissions and Student Accounts. Directs, trains, supervises and evaluates financial aid office staff and appropriate college offices regarding policies and updates to regulations. Assist Admissions with achieving enrollment goals. Researches, analyzes, develops and recommends departmental processes and procedures to increase/improve operational efficiency and to ensure proper controls and regulatory compliance. Oversees all program reviews and audits. Assist in the preparation of the annual FISAP, various surveys, waivers and grants. In addition, coordinates with the Institutional Researcher to complete financial aid portion of IPEDS. Monitor and maintain financial aid page on the SMWC website. Monitor and maintain the Financial Aid Policy & Procedure Manual. Develops, updates and presents financial aid information with brochures, literature, and workshops directed toward students, parents and community groups. Coordinates the development, implementation and maintenance of automated financial aid systems with the college IT staff and regulatory and guarantee agencies (Populi/Regent). Participates on college committees as required or assigned. Manages the student loan collection activities; and in collaboration with the Business Office, develops and directs a loan default prevention program. Ability to address and present information regarding financial aid, the College and its operation. Other duties as assigned Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree required; master\u2019s preferred. Must have 5-7 years of financial aid and supervision experience. Knowledge of Federal, local, and state programs that provide financial assistance to students\u2019 the principles of individual appraisal, including interviewing and advisement techniques; pertinent laws, rules and regulations; systems control auditing processes. Certified as a NASFAA FAAC preferred Must be a VA School Certifying Official (SCO) or obtain within 12 months. Demonstrated proficiency in the management of financial aid need analysis, packaging and required revision, interpreting Federal and state financial aid regulations. Demonstrated analytical, organizational and supervisory skills; strong counseling skills; gather and compile data and prepare reports; train, supervise, and evaluate the assigned staff. Strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. Knowledge and proficiency with Microsoft, spreadsheets. and working knowledge of data systems (Populi/Regent) preferred. Strong ethical and moral character. Strong commitment to excellent customer service. Working Conditions: High attention to detail and the ability to work in a multi-tasked, goal oriented and deadline driven environment. Must be self-motivated, able to work independently and as a member of an integrated team. Extensive sitting, walking and lifting may be required. Some travel and work a flexible schedule required."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4452404": {"title": "Student Employment - Social Media Content Creator \u2013 Kinesiology & Nursing", "description": "Student Employment - Social Media Content Creator \u2013 Kinesiology & Nursing. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description Saint Mary-of-the-Woods College (SMWC) is seeking a creative and motivated student worker to develop and manage the social media presence for the Kinesiology and Health Sciences (KHS) department, and the Nursing umbrella of programs. Following the recommendations of our recent KHS program review, along with the Nursing undergraduate and graduate program, this role focuses on boosting program recognition, increasing campus and online program viewership, and highlighting student faculty, and staff achievements. The ideal candidate is passionate about digital storytelling and eager to showcase the value of the KHS and Nursing programs to current students, prospective students, and the wider campus community. Essential Job Responsibilities \u00b7 Create, schedule, and publish engaging content across selected social media platforms to promote both programs. \u00b7 Photograph and film department activities, lab sessions, and special events for promotional use. \u00b7 Interview KHS and nursing students, faculty, staf, and alumni to feature their successes and stories. \u00b7 Monitor channel engagement, respond to comments professionally, and help grow total viewership. \u00b7 Collaborate with department leadership to ensure all content aligns with SMWC Vision, Mission, Values and Branding Guidelines. Other Duties & Responsibilities \u00b7 Maintain a basic content calendar to plan weekly or monthly posts. \u00b7 Other duties as assigned. Supervision \u00b7 Supervision Received: Works under direct supervision of the assigned KHS faculty and Program Support Specialist to the Division of Arts & Sciences. Requirements Current undergraduate/graduate student at SMWC. Dependable, punctual, and able to work independently or as part of a team. Willingness to learn and follow instructions. Positive attitude and strong work ethic. Basic familiarity with major social media platforms (such as Instagram, TikTok, or Facebook). Strong communication skills and basic visual design or photography skills."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4415004": {"title": "Student Employment - Le Fer Mailroom Clerk", "description": "Student Employment - Le Fer Mailroom Clerk. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description Responsible for receiving, sorting, processing, and distributing incoming and outgoing mail and packages for students, faculty, and staff. This position ensures accurate and timely delivery of correspondence while maintaining organized records and providing excellent customer service. If interested, please see Zac Warner, Director of Housing Requirements Strong Communication skills required Must have punctuality Professional demeanor required Limited computer skills required Knowledge of campus required Must be a SMWC student"}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4413083": {"title": "Student Employment - Equine Barn Worker", "description": "Student Employment - Equine Barn Worker. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description Feeding horses, cleaning stalls, barn maintenance, cleaning of barn, treating wounds/injuries on school horses. Must be available to stay and work over holidays. Supervisor: Angie McMillin Requirements Horse experience Ability to drive tractor Able to life over 50+ lbs"}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4261453": {"title": "Instructional Designer", "description": "Instructional Designer. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description Saint Mary-of-the-Woods College (SMWC), a Catholic liberal arts institution founded by the Sisters of Providence, seeks a collaborative and innovative Instructional Designer to support the development of high-quality, engaging, and inclusive learning experiences across all modalities\u2014online, hybrid, and face-to-face. The Instructional Designer works closely with faculty, academic leadership, and support staff to enhance teaching effectiveness and student learning through sound instructional design principles, technology integration, and pedagogical innovation. Essential Job Responsibilities: Collaborate with faculty to design, develop, and revise courses that align with institutional learning outcomes, accessibility standards, and best practices in teaching and learning. Support the effective use of the College\u2019s Learning Management System (Canvas) and other instructional technologies. Provide training, consultation, and resources to faculty in areas such as course design, assessment, online pedagogy, and digital tools. Develop and maintain templates, guides, and multimedia resources that promote consistency and quality in course delivery. Partner with the Center for Teaching and Learning, Academic Affairs, and Information Technology to advance initiatives in teaching excellence and innovation. Ensure all course materials meet accessibility and copyright compliance standards. Support evaluation and continuous improvement of online and hybrid programs through data collection, analysis, and faculty feedback. Stay current on trends and research in instructional design, learning science, educational technology, and higher education pedagogy. Perform other duties as assigned to support academic quality and student success. Supervision: Student Assistants and Academic Peers Working Conditions: This position is full-time and may allow for limited remote or hybrid work, depending on institutional needs. Occasional evening or weekend hours may be required for faculty training or special projects Requirements Required: Master\u2019s degree in Instructional Design, Educational Technology, Curriculum and Instruction, or a related field. Demonstrated experience designing and developing online and hybrid courses in a higher education setting. Proficiency with learning management systems (preferably Canvas), multimedia tools, and accessibility standards (e.g., ADA, Section 508, WCAG). Strong understanding of instructional design models such Quality Matters, or Universal Design for Learning (UDL). Excellent communication, collaboration, and project management skills. Preferred: Experience teaching in higher education. Familiarity with Catholic and liberal arts educational traditions. Experience developing faculty training or professional development programs. Knowledge of assessment design, data-informed improvement, and emerging educational technologies. Application Instructions Interested candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter addressing qualifications and commitment to SMWC\u2019s mission and values. R\u00e9sum\u00e9 or curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled."}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4114843": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Photography", "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Photography. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description Saint Mary-of-the-Woods College employs adjunct faculty who are student-centered individuals with a passion for teaching and student development. The adjunct is expected to demonstrate current content knowledge, methodologies, and skills. In addition, the adjunct is expected to be competent in pedagogy, assessment methods, and technology related to the learning systems utilized for both campus and online instruction. Regular and substantive interaction with students, as well as timely feedback, is expected. As a vital part of an academic program, the adjunct maintains collaborative relations with other faculty and administration. Essential Job Responsibilities: Excellent written and oral communication skills; professional and engaging demeanor with students, colleagues, staff, and administration. Instruct students in appropriate course content, provide experiential learning (if appropriate to the course), and guide students' work on assignments throughout the term. Clearly explain assignments, expectations, grading system, and method of preferred contact to students. Post and hold office hours (at least one hour per week per course), in-person and/or online Teach on campus during the scheduled class times, if in face-to-face format. Maintain, at minimum, weekly contact with students through such methods as discussion boards, synchronous instruction, or posted office hours (at least one hour per week per course) including the on-going use of Canvas, Teams, and SMWC email. Utilize the text and approved syllabi which includes student learning outcomes. Deliver courses that meet the ADA requirements for content and modules, and makes corrections as needed, and reports corrections to the Office of Student Success prior to the start of the term. Provide a list of required texts for this course to the Program Director/Chair at least 10 weeks prior to course delivery if applicable. Notify the Program Director/Chair and submit an Early Alert if a student is not maintaining contact or sufficient progress. Provide feedback on students' work in the form of graded assignments within 5 days of assignment submission. Submit reports or evaluations of students' progress when requested to do so by the Director/Chair. Enter grades in Canvas grade book for all students by the appropriate departmental or institutional date (if uncertain, discuss with the chair/director). Encourage students to complete the course evaluation at the end of the term. Adhere to the policies and procedures outlined in the SMWC Faculty Handbook and the College and/or Department Academic Integrity Policy. Other Duties & Responsibilities: Keep up-to date on policies and procedures within the Department and College by reading the posted Department Minutes. Supervision: Graduate student if assigned to the course. Clinical supervisors if assigned to the course. Preceptors if assigned to the course. Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree or higher in a related field according to program requirements Current credentials, such as licensure, if applicable See Expected Competencies below Experience with college-level teaching and course development Demonstrated experience incorporating technology in instructional practices. Experience using a learning management system such as Canvas"}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4090209": {"title": "Student Worker \u2013 Graduate Nursing Program", "description": "Student Worker \u2013 Graduate Nursing Program. Saint Mary-Of-The-Woods College. Description This position provides administrative and academic support to the Director of the Graduate Nursing Program and graduate nursing faculty in order to enhance program organization, communication, and effectiveness. Responsibilities Monitor weekly clinical hour submissions and verify compliance with required totals Maintain organized electronic files of all clinical forms (preceptor agreements, clinical evaluations, hours logs, etc.) Track student progression related to clinical requirements using provided templates Respond to general student inquiries via email and forward complex concerns to appropriate faculty Assist with scheduling and confirming clinical site visits with clinical faculty Assist with managing calendar invites for meetings involving the Director or faculty Perform basic data entry and support for student evaluations and surveys Compile and organize teaching resources or guides across multiple courses, including but not limited to obtaining desk copies and communication with textbook and other curriculum representatives Assist in compiling handbooks and orientation materials Support live and virtual events for graduate nursing students Help gather data on program outcomes in cooperation with the Program Director Assist the Director with program marketing and engagement activities, including but not limited to scheduling outreach activities, developing and maintaining a strong, appropriate social media presence, and promoting a graduate culture. This may include, but is not limited to, assisting with quality improvement activities, collecting data, etc. Other duties as assigned Requirements Preferred Qualifications Strong organizational and communication skills Proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, Canvas and social media platforms Ability to work independently and maintain confidentiality Hours & Compensation Approximately 8-10 hours per week The position begins Summer session 2026"}}, "rows": {"https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4529532": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4529532", "job_title_in_post": "People and Payroll Specialist", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3982553": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3982553", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Director of Student Success", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Student Success", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4510227": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4510227", "job_title_in_post": "Director of Financial Aid", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Financial Aid", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4452404": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4452404", "job_title_in_post": "Student Employment - Social Media Content Creator \u2013 Kinesiology & Nursing", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Division of Arts & Sciences", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4415004": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4415004", "job_title_in_post": "Student Employment - Le Fer Mailroom Clerk", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4413083": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4413083", "job_title_in_post": "Student Employment - Equine Barn Worker", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4261453": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4261453", "job_title_in_post": "Instructional Designer", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "higher education pedagogy; educational technology", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4114843": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4114843", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor - Photography", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Photography", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4090209": {"school_id": 449, "posting_url": "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4090209", "job_title_in_post": "Student Worker \u2013 Graduate Nursing Program", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 449, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:42:59+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:42:59+00:00", "last_error": ""}